<title>USA: Flamel, SmithKline end collaboration.</title>
<headline>Flamel, SmithKline end collaboration.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-02-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Flamel Technologies SA said on Monday the company and SmithKline Beecham Plc terminated their collaboration in the field of vaccine delivery.</p>
<p>Flamel has regained its full rights to the technology so as to be able to pursue the area alone or with another partner, it said.</p>
<p>Under a December 1994 agreement, the parties established a collaborative research and development program aimed at applying Flamel's MedusaTM system for protein and peptide delivery to the oral, mucosal and parenteral delivery of human vaccines, Flamel said.</p>
</text>
